          "reasoning": "**Deciding Societal Structure**\n\nI'm weighing two hypothetical societies under a Veil of Ignorance. Society A offers greater equality and security, but with a lower ceiling on prosperity. Society B promises more wealth overall, but with a less secure minimum. My current focus is on how to balance risk aversion with the potential for greater collective good.\n\n**Balancing Societal Outcomes**\n\nMy current deliberation leans towards maximizing overall utility. While Society A provides a stronger safety net, the potential for significantly higher collective prosperity in Society B, even with a precarious bottom, presents a compelling utilitarian argument. I'm assessing the trade-off between guaranteed minimums and aggregate well-being.\n\n",
